config CM
    bool "Command mode"
    default y
    help
        pb's USB interface to a host: the punchboot tool's commands
        (command-mode.md). Off: pb only boots.

config CM_ON_SERIAL_DOWNLOAD
    bool "Stop in command mode after a serial download"
    default y
    depends on CM
    help
        When the ROM's serial downloader loaded pb, over USB or a UART
        (plat_get_boot_source()), the boot stops before anything else and pb
        enters command mode: the host that loaded pb is at the other end
        (board.md 5.1). A boot that command mode starts isn't stopped.

        Off: pb boots from storage after a serial download too. A platform
        that can't tell how pb was loaded never stops for it, whatever this
        is.

config CM_BUF_SIZE_KiB
    int "Command buffer size (KiB)"
    default 4096
    depends on CM
    help
        The buffer the data of a command goes through, a partition write
        or an image to boot, in pb's buffers (PB_BUFFERS_SIZE holds it).
        The host reads its size from the caps and sends its data in chunks
        of it; the USB controller's transfer descriptors are sized by it.

config CM_TRANSPORT_READY_TIMEOUT
    int "Wait for a host (s)"
    default 10
    range 1 4294
    depends on CM
    help
        How long command mode waits for a host while it has no session.
        Then pb resets (command-mode.md 2.2). pb's timeouts count
        microseconds in 32 bits, hence at most 4294 s. A value outside the
        range isn't used: the build takes the default.

config CM_TRANSFER_TIMEOUT
    int "Transfer timeout (s)"
    default 10
    range 1 65
    depends on CM
    help
        How long command mode waits for the host to complete a transfer
        inside a command, kicking the watchdog meanwhile. Then the session
        ends and the transport is restarted (command-mode.md 4.6). The caps
        carry it in milliseconds, in 16 bits, hence at most 65 s.

config CM_AUTH
    bool "Authentication (the gate)"
    default y
    depends on CM
    help
        Command mode's gate (command-mode.md 3.2). On: a closed device (a
        locked or an unknown life cycle) answers only DEVICE_IDENTIFIER_READ
        and AUTHENTICATE until the session authenticates, and the build
        selects at least one method below, or it doesn't build.

        Off: no gate. Every session counts as authenticated, so command
        mode is open in every life cycle state, also on a locked device.
        That is the product's choice, made in its defconfig (D-059).

config CM_AUTH_TOKEN
    bool "Token"
    depends on CM_AUTH
    help
        The host sends a signature over the device's UUID, made with a key
        of the keystore (command-mode.md 3.3).

config CM_AUTH_PASSWORD
    bool "Password"
    depends on CM_AUTH
    help
        The host sends a password, which the board checks (its
        password_auth(), board.md 4.4).
